{
 "summary": "Findings: Four defects require plan changes: invalid numbers reach the gateway, the post-send marker does not guarantee once-only delivery, email failures suppress SMS, and the time-zone tests cannot detect UTC formatting.",
 "files_modified": [],
 "findings": [
  {
   "Title": "normalizePhone does not validate mobile numbers or return null",
   "Severity": "P1",
   "Location": "phase-2/t1 (plan.md:77,83-86); context.key_files (plan.md:9)",
   "Failure": "The plan treats normalization as validation and sends every non-null result. src/patients/phone.ts:1-4 only removes punctuation and returns string, never null. Patient.mobile contains registration input, not validated data (src/patients/patients.ts:5-6). A fresh probe returned \"12345\" unchanged, \"notanumber\" for \"not a number\", and \"\" for empty input. All pass the planned non-null guard, violating REQUEST.md:7 and triggering billable attempts (src/sms/gateway.ts:1-3). The claimed E.164 conversion is also absent: \"07700 900123\" becomes \"07700900123\". The gateway interface does not specify E.164 requirements.",
   "Fix": "Replace the false helper premise with an explicit mobile-validation and gateway-formatting design. Specify supported regions for national-format input. Add the required implementation files and validation tests, including malformed inputs and non-mobile numbers. Verify that invalid inputs cause zero gateway calls."
  },
  {
   "Title": "The post-send marker cannot guarantee at-most-once delivery",
   "Severity": "P1",
   "Location": "phase-2/t1 (plan.md:77,88); summary and constraints (plan.md:3,19); success_criteria (plan.md:98)",
   "Failure": "The plan inserts SMS after email but before markReminded. A rejected SMS therefore leaves an already-emailed appointment unmarked; another overlapping pass repeats the email. If marking fails after both sends, both can repeat. The existing control flow awaits delivery before marking and catches failures without marking (src/reminders/pass.ts:30-41). The store selects unmarked appointments (src/appointments.ts:10-13; tests/fakes.ts:19-24). A fresh probe against the current pass, with markReminded rejecting, ran at 09:20 and 09:25 for the same due appointment and recorded two emails. The claimed existing invariant is false, and the successful second-pass scenario does not establish REQUEST.md:8.",
   "Fix": "Specify a failure-safe once-per-appointment delivery/consumption protocol before implementation. Include any required persistence or channel-contract changes rather than assuming the marker suffices. Add failure-path verification for SMS rejection after email success and marker failure after sending, with no repeated messages."
  },
  {
   "Title": "An email failure prevents an eligible patient's SMS attempt",
   "Severity": "P2",
   "Location": "phase-2/t1 (plan.md:77,83-88)",
   "Failure": "The planned SMS runs only after the awaited email inside the existing appointment-level try block. If email rejects, control jumps to reportFailure and skips the SMS (src/reminders/pass.ts:28-41), despite the patient's valid mobile number. A fresh probe confirmed that email rejection exits the body before markReminded and reports the appointment failure. This is a supported failure path documented by ReminderDeps.reportFailure (src/reminders/pass.ts:12-13). The plan neither resolves this channel coupling against the every-valid-mobile requirement (REQUEST.md:7) nor tests it.",
   "Fix": "Specify how each channel is attempted when the other fails, consistently with the once-only protocol. Do not make the SMS attempt depend on email success. Add an email-rejection case that verifies the eligible SMS attempt and the intended failure reporting."
  },
  {
   "Title": "The proposed local-time assertions also pass with UTC formatting",
   "Severity": "P2",
   "Location": "phase-1/t1 (plan.md:47-49); phase-1/t2 (plan.md:54-59); implementation_contract/d1 (plan.md:106-108)",
   "Failure": "Every proposed time-zone fixture uses Europe/London on 12 January 2027. A fresh Intl probe produced 09:30 for both London and UTC at that instant. The current UTC-only formatter (src/format.ts:2-14) already returns the proposed expected string, which is the existing assertion (tests/format.test.ts:4-5). The pass fixture uses the same zone and January date (tests/pass.test.ts:5,11). Thus the formatter could ignore the new parameter, or a channel could use UTC, without failing these checks. Naming a clinic zone does not prove the requested localization.",
   "Fix": "Use a fixture whose clinic offset is nonzero at the appointment instant, such as London in summer or Denver in winter. Assert the exact localized output in the formatter, email, and SMS so retained UTC behavior fails."
  }
 ],
 "evidence_notes": [
  "Reviewed all supplied production files and tests, plus REQUEST.md, README.md, package.json, and the complete plan. No AGENTS.md exists in the supplied tree.",
  "Confirmed the single production formatSlot caller at src/reminders/pass.ts:34, the UTC implementation at src/format.ts:4, clinic timeZone at src/clinics.ts:4-5, injected channels at src/reminders/pass.ts:7-13, and fake email recording at tests/fakes.ts:37.",
  "The claim that SmsGateway is already used for sign-in codes is stated in README.md:8 but cannot be verified against implementation code in this snapshot. src/sms/gateway.ts:1-4 contains only an interface; no sign-in caller or provider implementation is supplied. No real provider behavior or E.164 requirement was verified.",
  "Verification used read-only Bun probes against the current exported functions and Intl. No files were changed and no test suite was run."
 ]
}

{
 "summary": "Findings: two P1 defects prevent the plan from meeting the request. The updatedAt-only selector misses payment status changes, and advancing the watermark before upload loses changes after a failed upload.",
 "files_modified": [],
 "findings": [
  {
   "Title": "Payment status changes are invisible to the proposed selector",
   "Severity": "P1",
   "Location": "phase-1/t1 (plan.md:37-45), also context.key_files (plan.md:7) and phase-2/t1 (plan.md:77)",
   "Failure": "The plan claims every store write stamps updatedAt. In fact, create initializes it and officer updates advance it (src/members.ts:22-33), but setStatus only replaces status and retains the previous timestamp (src/members.ts:37-41). The timestamp deliberately means the last officer edit (src/members.ts:11-12). For a member whose updatedAt precedes the last export watermark, a subsequent payment status change therefore fails the proposed updatedAt filter. Both lapsed and cancelled can follow this path (src/members.ts:2,38-40). This violates REQUEST.md:9. The existing test explicitly protects the unchanged timestamp after setStatus (tests/members.test.ts:4-14), and it passes.",
   "Fix": "Replace the updatedAt-only selection design with change tracking that observes payment status writes while preserving the officer-edit timestamp contract. Specify how that tracking works with the unchanged-store constraint. Require export-job tests that perform a successful export, call the real MemberStore.setStatus for lapsed and cancelled, and verify that the next export includes those members."
  },
  {
   "Title": "The watermark advances even when the upload fails",
   "Severity": "P1",
   "Location": "phase-2/t1 (plan.md:77-85); related acceptance omissions at plan.md:104-108,115-116",
   "Failure": "The specified order stores startedAt before uploading. The real client throws FederationError for a rejected HTTP response (src/federation/client.ts:10-16), and the Settings port exposes independent get/set operations with no rollback mechanism (src/settings.ts:2-4). The plan specifies no restoration after failure. On the next invocation, the advanced watermark excludes failed-upload members whose updatedAt is earlier than startedAt. The scheduler's documented next-night retry reruns the job, not the original payload (src/scheduler.ts:3-5). This directly violates the last-successful-export boundary and failed-upload retry requirements in REQUEST.md:7,10. None of the planned job tests covers upload failure.",
   "Fix": "Keep the run-start timestamp, but persist it only after the awaited upload succeeds. Leave the previous watermark intact when the upload rejects. Add first-export and incremental-export failure tests that verify the unchanged watermark and inclusion of all failed changes on the following night's successful run. Include this requirement in the success criteria and completion checks."
  }
 ],
 "verification": {
  "command": "bun test tests/members.test.ts",
  "result": "Passed: 1 test, 3 assertions, 0 failures.",
  "scope": "Confirmed the existing MemberStore timestamp contract. No project files were changed."
 },
 "claim_audit_notes": [
  "The plan's claim that create and officer update stamp updatedAt is supported by src/members.ts:22-33; its extension of that claim to setStatus is refuted by src/members.ts:37-41.",
  "Settings is an asynchronous string key-value port (src/settings.ts:2-4). Restart persistence and the SQLite adapter are documented at src/settings.ts:1, but no adapter implementation is supplied; actual runtime durability is UNVERIFIED.",
  "FederationClient.uploadMembers accepts a CSV string and returns Promise<void> (src/federation/client.ts:3-5). The HTTP adapter posts text/csv to /registry/members and throws FederationError for a non-success response (src/federation/client.ts:10-16).",
  "Scheduler.nightly accepts a name and asynchronous job (src/scheduler.ts:1-5). The 02:00 schedule, logging, and next-night rerun are interface documentation only (src/scheduler.ts:4); actual runtime scheduling and error handling are UNVERIFIED because no scheduler implementation is supplied.",
  "The request's column order matches the planned CSV header (REQUEST.md:8; plan.md:52). Member provides the corresponding id, name, membershipType, and status fields (src/members.ts:4-9). MemberStore.all returns the readonly member array accepted by the proposed selector (src/members.ts:50-51; plan.md:37).",
  "The asserted existing conventions for job deps objects and dotted Settings keys (plan.md:14-15) have no supplied examples. The complete source tree contains only members.ts, settings.ts, scheduler.ts, and federation/client.ts; Settings accepts arbitrary string keys (src/settings.ts:3-4). These conventions are unsubstantiated, although the proposed API and key remain compatible with the supplied ports."
 ]
}

{
 "summary": "Findings: Three defects. The plan omits account store credit, leaves the nightly importer incompatible with the required destination parameter, and rejects an explicit original destination at the till boundary.",
 "findings": [
  {
   "Title": "The third required destination, customer-account store credit, is missing",
   "Severity": "P1",
   "Location": "phase-1/t1, phase-1/t2, phase-2/t1; plan.md:41,51,80,97-101",
   "Failure": "REQUEST.md:7-12 requires three destinations, including store credit only for sales made to a customer account. The planned persisted and request unions contain only original and gift-card destinations, and the route rejects other values. The success criteria also omit store credit. The necessary account identity already exists at src/sales.ts:17-18. CreditStore and addStoreCredit already provide the balance update at src/customers/credit.ts:1-10. Therefore, following every planned task still cannot deliver a required destination or enforce its account-eligibility rule.",
   "Fix": "Add store credit to the request and persisted destination models. Use the sale's customerId and the existing addStoreCredit helper; reject this destination when the sale has no customer account. Include dependency wiring, route handling, and tests for eligible sales, ineligible sales without side effects, recorded destination, and unchanged amount limits. Add store credit to the success criteria."
  },
  {
   "Title": "The required destination parameter leaves the nightly refund caller unmigrated",
   "Severity": "P2",
   "Location": "phase-1/t2; plan.md:51-56; implementation_contract/d1 at plan.md:108-109",
   "Failure": "The plan changes refundSale to require a fourth argument, but its files and tasks omit src/jobs/returns-import.ts. That job imports refundSale and RefundDeps at src/jobs/returns-import.ts:1 and still calls refundSale with three arguments at src/jobs/returns-import.ts:20. The current public signature accepts three arguments at src/payments/refunds.ts:23. Updating the till and direct refund tests does not resolve this incompatible production call. The existing importer test checks counts and rejected sale IDs, but not gateway calls or recorded destinations (tests/returns-import.test.ts:5-12).",
   "Fix": "Prefer a default original destination in refundSale to preserve the existing three-argument contract. If the required argument remains, explicitly migrate the importer to original-method refunds in the same phase. Extend its existing test to verify the gateway call and original destination, and include that test in phase-1 verification."
  },
  {
   "Title": "The till parser rejects the supported explicit original destination",
   "Severity": "P2",
   "Location": "phase-2/t1; plan.md:80-89",
   "Failure": "The parser accepts an absent destination or a gift-card destination and declares every other value a 400. This rejects { kind: \"original\" }, although phase-1/t2 explicitly includes it in RefundRequestDestination (plan.md:51). REQUEST.md:7-9 makes the original method a selectable destination as well as the default. The existing route has no destination parser to supply a separate acceptance path: it currently extracts only amountCents and calls refundSale (src/till/routes.ts:13-24). The listed route tests cover omission but not explicit original selection.",
   "Fix": "Accept { kind: \"original\" } explicitly, alongside the omitted-field default. Add a route test that supplies this destination and asserts a 201 response, the original gateway refund, and the recorded original destination."
  }
 ],
 "files_modified": []
}

{
 "summary": "Findings: The plan changes retainer billing, omits the monthly statement consumer, leaves a billed-hours precision conflict unresolved, and adds a misleading note to retainer invoices. No files were changed.",
 "files_modified": [],
 "findings": [
  {
   "Title": "Retainer entries would incorrectly receive six-minute rounding",
   "Severity": "P1",
   "Location": "phase-1/t1 and phase-1/t2 (plan.md:40,53)",
   "Failure": "REQUEST.md:7-8 requires six-minute rounding only for standard clients and preserves whole-minute billing for retainers. Client already exposes this distinction at src/clients.ts:4. The proposed billedTenths(entry) cannot inspect the client plan, and t2 applies it unconditionally. A seven-minute retainer entry at 12000 cents/hour would therefore cost 2400 cents instead of the existing 1400 cents computed by src/billing/invoice.ts:23-28. The planned tests contain no retainer case.",
   "Fix": "Make the shared billing calculation plan-aware. Preserve whole-minute hours and charges for retainers, and add invoice tests that distinguish the two plans using non-multiple-of-six durations."
  },
  {
   "Title": "Deleting billableMinutes leaves the monthly statement unresolved and unimplemented",
   "Severity": "P1",
   "Location": "phase-1/t1 and phase-1 file list (plan.md:31-40)",
   "Failure": "The claim that billableMinutes has only the invoice caller is false. src/reports/statement.ts:3 imports it, and src/reports/statement.ts:15-17 uses it to calculate monthly hours. Neither phase includes that consumer. Deleting the export leaves its import unresolved; merely retaining the old helper would leave statements on unrounded minutes, contrary to REQUEST.md:10. The existing standard-client statement fixture contains 90 and 45 minutes and expects 2.25 hours (tests/statement.test.ts:4-12); the planned invoice rounding produces 2.30 hours for those entries.",
   "Fix": "Include src/reports/statement.ts and tests/statement.test.ts in phase-1. Apply the same plan-aware per-entry billing calculation before monthly aggregation, preserve client/month filtering, update the fixture, and verify invoice/statement agreement with multiple rounded entries. Migrate all helper consumers before removing an export."
  },
  {
   "Title": "The plan leaves whole-minute display precision inconsistent across documents",
   "Severity": "P2",
   "Location": "phase-1/t2 and context.constraints (plan.md:19,53); success_criteria (plan.md:93-97)",
   "Failure": "Correcting the retainer branch and sharing billed minutes would still not prove REQUEST.md:10. Invoice hours round each entry to two decimals at src/billing/invoice.ts:27, while statements round only the monthly sum at src/reports/statement.ts:16-17. A fresh probe of both production functions with two one-minute retainer entries produced invoice lines of 0.02 and 0.02 hours, totaling 0.04, but a statement of 0.03 hours. The plan preserves two-decimal invoice lines without specifying how documents will agree for retained whole-minute billing.",
   "Fix": "Specify how the invoice and statement will present matching billed hours while preserving retainer minute-based charges. Add an acceptance case with multiple one-minute retainer entries; sharing the rounding helper alone is insufficient."
  },
  {
   "Title": "The increment note is applied to retainer invoices too",
   "Severity": "P2",
   "Location": "phase-2/t1 (plan.md:79-85)",
   "Failure": "The task sets notes unconditionally, although REQUEST.md:11 assigns this note to standard-client invoices. buildInvoice receives a Client at src/billing/invoice.ts:21, and Client.plan identifies retainers at src/clients.ts:4. Once whole-minute retainer billing is preserved, the proposed note falsely tells those clients that their time receives six-minute rounding. The existing notes list is empty at src/billing/invoice.ts:35.",
   "Fix": "Add the exact note only for standard clients. Test its presence on standard invoices and its absence on retainer invoices."
  }
 ]
}

{
 "summary": "Findings: The proposed page invalidation cannot work with the actual cache API. The plan also has two verification gaps.",
 "findings": [
  {
   "Title": "Invalidate the complete page keys, not a nonexistent prefix key",
   "Severity": "P1",
   "Location": "phase-1/t1 and phase-1/t2; plan.md:9,38,48",
   "Failure": "The plan claims invalidate(prefix) removes matching entries. It actually deletes exactly one key (src/cache.ts:26-29). renderPage stores entries under page:<slug>:html and page:<slug>:print (src/render.ts:20-24,30). Consequently, invalidating page:<slug> removes neither entry, and both views remain stale. A fresh Bun probe using the proposed invalidation calls returned the old title and body in both views while the section indexes updated.",
   "Fix": "Replace pageCachePrefix with a shared exact-key builder that accepts the slug and view. Invalidate the html and print keys explicitly after saving. Keep TtlCache.invalidate's existing exact-key contract."
  },
  {
   "Title": "Warm both section indexes before testing a move",
   "Severity": "P2",
   "Location": "phase-1/t2; plan.md:53-58",
   "Failure": "The move scenario does not require caching either section before saving. A cold-cache test passes even without section invalidation: renderSectionIndex reads the current PageStore on a cache miss (src/render.ts:35-41), and PageStore.inSection filters the newly saved section (src/pages.ts:15-20). Such a test does not prove that either previously cached index updates, as REQUEST.md:8 requires.",
   "Fix": "Render both source and destination indexes before moving the page. Save the move, then verify that the source loses the page and the destination gains it without advancing the cache clock."
  },
  {
   "Title": "Replace the unavailable browser verification with a runnable check",
   "Severity": "P2",
   "Location": "phase-1; plan.md:63",
   "Failure": "The qualitative check requires running a handbook application, opening browser views, and editing through a UI. This project supplies no application launcher or browser surface. Its only package script runs tests (package.json:5-7); the relevant entrypoints are savePage and the rendering functions (src/editor.ts:6-11; src/render.ts:20-42). The planned manual procedure cannot be executed against this repository.",
   "Fix": "Use the planned editor integration tests as the final acceptance check through savePage, renderPage, and renderSectionIndex. Remove the unavailable browser procedure rather than adding an application outside the request."
  }
 ],
 "files_modified": []
}

{
 "summary": "Findings: Two release blockers and two verification gaps. Phase 1 queries a column introduced only in phase 2. Phase 2 cannot migrate an existing database with the current runner. Production bin persistence and the promised type check lack verification.",
 "files_modified": [],
 "findings": [
  {
   "Title": "Deploy the bin column before the first query that reads it",
   "Severity": "P1",
   "Location": "phase-1/t1; phase-2/t1",
   "Failure": "Phase 1 selects i.bin_code (plan.md:42), but phase 2 introduces that column (plan.md:82). These phases deploy separately (plan.md:21). The current items table has only sku and name (migrations/001_items.sql:1-4), and production reads it through SqlItemRepo.linesForOrder (src/items.ts:25-34). Each merge immediately deploys, and picking runs around the clock (README.md:13). A fresh Bun/SQLite probe against the current migrated schema confirmed that the planned query fails with 'no such column: i.bin_code'. Thus phase 1 breaks the production pick list rather than displaying '-'.",
   "Fix": "Include the schema migration in the same deployment as the first bin-code query, or deploy the migration earlier. Keep the clerk endpoint later if desired. Verify phase 1 against SqlItemRepo and its deployed schema before merging."
  },
  {
   "Title": "Provide an upgrade path that does not replay existing migrations",
   "Severity": "P1",
   "Location": "phase-2/t1",
   "Failure": "The plan adds an unconditional ALTER TABLE and checks only an empty database (plan.md:82-87). However, migrate executes every SQL file on every call without tracking applied migrations (src/db.ts:8-11). Existing migrations use unconditional CREATE TABLE statements (migrations/001_items.sql:1-4; migrations/002_order_lines.sql:1-7). On an existing production database, migration 001 fails before migration 003 runs. A fresh probe confirmed that calling migrate again on a populated migrated database throws 'table items already exists'. Empty-database tests conceal this because the existing SQL test creates a fresh database each time (tests/sql-item-repo.test.ts:8-12).",
   "Fix": "Add the smallest explicit migration mechanism that applies only pending migrations, including initialization for an existing installation. Verify an upgrade from the current populated schema, preservation of existing rows, null bins for existing items, and a subsequent deployment with no pending migrations."
  },
  {
   "Title": "Verify bin reads and writes through the production SQL repository",
   "Severity": "P2",
   "Location": "phase-2/t2; phase-2/t3; phase-2 verification",
   "Failure": "The new SQL update receives only validator tests (plan.md:92-100); set/clear route tests use MemoryItemRepo (plan.md:105-114). No phase updates tests/sql-item-repo.test.ts. That existing test checks only lineNo, sku, name, and quantity (tests/sql-item-repo.test.ts:17-22), so it cannot catch incorrect bin mapping. MemoryItemRepo stores order-line fixtures rather than querying the items table (tests/memory-item-repo.ts:3-7), so its updates cannot prove SQL persistence or item-based lookup. Consequently 'bun test' can pass while the production bin implementation is incorrect.",
   "Fix": "Extend tests/sql-item-repo.test.ts to cover null and populated bin reads, setting and clearing an existing item, and false for an unknown SKU. Include an existing item without order lines so the item-level setter contract is verified independently of the memory fixture model."
  },
  {
   "Title": "Add an executable check for the promised type-check scenario",
   "Severity": "P2",
   "Location": "phase-1/t1; phase-1 verification",
   "Failure": "The plan promises that the project type-checks after adding the required PickLine field (plan.md:42-47), but its verification command only runs Bun tests (plan.md:64). The package defines only a test command, with no type-check gate (package.json:5-7). This matters because the SQL result uses an explicit PickLineRow type that currently lacks bin_code (src/items.ts:15-20,27), and rendering fixtures must satisfy PickLine (tests/memory-item-repo.ts:1-4; tests/picklist.test.ts:6-10). A fresh Bun probe executed a TypeScript assignment with an incompatible declared type without rejecting it, confirming that execution does not establish type correctness.",
   "Fix": "Specify a runnable TypeScript type-check command and its required configuration in the phase verification. Use it to verify the updated row type, interface implementations, and fixtures in addition to running behavior tests."
  }
 ],
 "verified_nondefects": [
  "The named repository files and current architecture match the plan: SQL is in SqlItemRepo, routes and rendering use ItemRepo, and MemoryItemRepo supplies sorted whole PickLine fixtures (src/items.ts:10-35; src/picklist.ts:1-8; src/routes.ts:1-11; tests/memory-item-repo.ts:1-8).",
  "The proposed bin expression accepted A-03-2 and rejected every listed malformed example in a fresh Bun probe; tested trailing line terminators were also rejected.",
  "A fresh Bun/SQLite probe confirmed that the proposed UPDATE reports one changed row for setting, repeating the same value, and clearing an existing SKU, and zero for an unknown SKU."
 ]
}

{
 "summary": "Findings: one dependency-contract regression and one incorrect legacy-data interpretation. All referenced source files, existing callers, migrations, and tests were inspected. No project files were changed.",
 "files_modified": [],
 "findings": [
  {
   "Title": "Keep the renewal clock out of the existing purchase dependency contract",
   "Severity": "P2",
   "Location": "phase-2/t2 (plan.md:93)",
   "Failure": "The plan adds a required today function to PortalDeps. That exported interface is also the input contract for the existing postNewPermit function (src/routes.ts:4-8,27). The existing purchase caller supplies no clock (tests/routes.test.ts:8-11), and purchasing does not use one (src/routes.ts:28-39). The change therefore breaks an existing caller's TypeScript contract for a dependency needed only by the new renewal operation.",
   "Fix": "Leave PortalDeps unchanged. Require today only in postRenewal's dependency type, for example through an intersection with PortalDeps. This preserves existing purchase callers without adding a wrapper."
  },
  {
   "Title": "Do not interpret a legacy NULL as proof that the permit was never renewed",
   "Severity": "P3",
   "Location": "phase-1/t1 (plan.md:42)",
   "Failure": "The plan defines NULL as meaning the permit has not been renewed since purchase, while assigning NULL to every existing row without a backfill. Existing rows contain only the expiry, not renewal history (migrations/001_permits.sql:1-8; src/permits.ts:4-10). The request describes an existing town-hall renewal process (REQUEST.md:5). The available data therefore cannot distinguish a never-renewed permit from a previously renewed permit whose renewal date was not recorded.",
   "Fix": "Define NULL as no known or recorded renewal date. Explicitly distinguish unknown legacy history from a new purchase that has not yet been renewed. Do not promise historical dates without an identified source."
  }
 ],
 "verification": [
  "bun test tests/dates.test.ts: 2 passed, 0 failed; confirmed the plan's existing calendar-arithmetic examples.",
  "bun test tests/sql-permit-repo.test.ts: 1 passed, 0 failed; confirmed the current SQL repository round-trip and replacement behavior."
 ],
 "evidence_limits": [
  "Payment-service deduplication, nightly refunds, and deployment ordering are documented contracts (src/payments.ts:3-5; README.md:13,17), not runtime behavior verified against supplied implementations.",
  "The supplied project contains no clerks' report implementation or staging entry point. The plan's staging report check remains unverified."
 ]
}

{
 "summary": "Findings: five defects. The plan uses a non-validator to authorize billed SMS attempts, does not guarantee one reminder pass, suppresses SMS after email failures, tests only a zero-offset time zone, and assigns conflicting meanings to the fake's sms property.",
 "files_modified": [],
 "findings": [
  {
   "Title": "The proposed phone check authorizes invalid numbers",
   "Severity": "P1",
   "Location": "phase-2/t1; plan.md:9,77,83-87",
   "Failure": "The plan assumes normalizePhone returns E.164 or null. In fact, src/patients/phone.ts:1-4 only removes punctuation and always returns a string. Patient.mobile is unvalidated registration input (src/patients/patients.ts:5-6). A fresh runtime probe confirmed that \"12345\", \"abc\", and an empty string all pass the proposed non-null check; \"07700 900123\" remains \"07700900123\", without international normalization. The planned invalid-number test will fail, and the gateway bills every attempt (src/sms/gateway.ts:1-3), violating REQUEST.md:7.",
   "Fix": "Add an explicit mobile-validation and international-normalization design before gateway invocation. Specify the country context for national inputs, distinguish mobile numbers from landlines, and identify the implementation and tests. Preserve normalizePhone's existing contract unless its change is explicitly addressed. Test valid formatted inputs, invalid inputs, and non-mobile numbers, asserting zero gateway attempts for rejected inputs."
  },
  {
   "Title": "The post-send marker does not guarantee at most one reminder pass",
   "Severity": "P1",
   "Location": "phase-2/t1; plan.md:3,19,77,88,98",
   "Failure": "The plan treats markReminded after both sends as an at-most-once guarantee. The current code sends email before marking, and catches failures without recording that an attempt occurred (src/reminders/pass.ts:30-40). The store selects appointments without remindedAt (src/appointments.ts:11-13; tests/fakes.ts:19-24). A fresh probe with an injected markReminded rejection sent two emails across the same overlapping times used by the existing test. Adding SMS before the marker preserves this duplicate path and introduces another failure point after email delivery. The happy-path second-pass test does not prove REQUEST.md:8.",
   "Fix": "Specify how an appointment's single pass is durably consumed before outbound attempts, including failed sends and failed persistence. Update the store contract and affected files if required. Add failure-path verification that a later eligible invocation cannot resend either channel. Do not claim at-most-once behavior from the existing post-send marker."
  },
  {
   "Title": "An email failure prevents the SMS attempt",
